# Project Context

This is a Go backend for a service marketplace application.

The system has:
- Customer mobile app
- Provider mobile app
- Admin web dashboard
- Public website
- Go backend API
- PostgreSQL database
- WebSocket notifications
- Push notifications
- Payment gateway integration
- Modular monolith architecture

# Architecture Rules

Use modular monolith architecture.

Each business module should contain:
- handler.go
- service.go
- repository.go
- model.go
- dto.go
- routes.go

Do not create microservices unless explicitly requested.

Keep business logic inside service layer.

Handlers should only:
- parse request
- validate input
- call service
- return response

Repositories should only:
- query database
- map database result

# Code Quality Rules

Write simple Go code.

Prefer clear code over clever code.

Use context.Context in service and repository methods.

Return typed errors from business logic.

Do not panic in normal application flow.

Do not put business logic in main.go.

Use dependency injection through constructors.

# Security Rules

Never hardcode secrets.

Use environment variables for:
- database URL
- JWT secret
- payment keys
- Firebase keys
- SMTP keys

Never expose internal error details to API users.

Validate all request bodies.

Check authentication and authorization before modifying data.

# Output Rules

When generating code:
- include file path
- include complete code
- explain where to place it
- mention required commands